diff --git a/docs/CSA_SUFFIX_PRUNING.md b/docs/CSA_SUFFIX_PRUNING.md
new file mode 100644
index 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000..9d124e6d25a57c2757daf6150fe1f5013308484f
--- /dev/null
+++ b/docs/CSA_SUFFIX_PRUNING.md
@@ -0,0 +1,121 @@
+# Public CSA destination suffix feasibility certificate
+
+Status: generic correctness candidate, not a measured Singapore optimization result.
+The official, current, complete LTA bus + rail data gate remains open. No SG
+performance campaign was run for this candidate, and no speed/convergence claim
+is made. The earlier community-feed/70-known-footpath pilot is provisional only.
+
+## What changes
+
+Only public `csa` exact-top-k searches gain an optional destination-directed,
+boarding-layered temporal suffix infeasibility test. It is used by Single,
+Shared, StratifiedSingle and StratifiedShared. Full enumeration and heuristic
+per-stop modes do not use it. K, label/journey budgets, horizon, walking limits,
+accessibility, transfer semantics and output identity ordering are unchanged.
+The existing last-boarding walking/vehicle bound remains in place.
+
+A label is pruned only when no destination suffix exists even in a relaxation
+of the requested problem. A ride/walk transition proved hopeless is rejected
+before allocating a label. This is consistent with the existing definition of
+MaxLabels as generated labels and the existing final-boarding preallocation
+prune. ConnectionAttempts/FootpathAttempts continue to count attempted work;
+DeadEndPruned includes the new proof as well as the existing final-boarding proof.
+
+## Recurrence and proof
+
+Let T be LatestArrival, D the destination, and L_b(s) the latest nonnegative
+ready-to-board time at stop s from which a relaxed suffix can reach D by T with
+at most b additional vehicle boardings. Missing values are -1. The relaxation
+retains directed footpaths, fixed event times, pickup/dropoff, trip-sequence
+continuation and the boarding count. It ignores accessibility, transfer
+rules/buffers, total/phase walking resources and leg count. Ignoring these
+restrictions only adds possible suffixes.
+
+L_0(s) is T minus the directed shortest walking distance s -> D, or -1 when
+that value is negative/unreachable. Reverse Dijkstra uses incoming directed
+footpaths; it never reverses a walk's feasible direction.
+
+For a connection c_i in a valid contiguous trip chain and r additional
+boardings after that already-boarded connection, define R_r(c_i) by reverse
+sequence traversal:
+
+    R_r(c_i) = (Dropoff(c_i) and Arrival(c_i) <= L_r(To(c_i)))
+               or R_r(c_(i+1)).
+
+The final connection has no next term. Dataset validation guarantees spatial
+and temporal trip continuity. Therefore the next term is a valid stay-aboard
+possibility, independent of intermediate pickup/dropoff flags. This also
+handles equal-time / zero-duration events regardless of connection ID order.
+
+For b >= 1, ready-to-board seeds are:
+
+    P_b(s) = max(L_(b-1)(s),
+                 Departure(c) for c with From(c)=s, Pickup(c), R_(b-1)(c)).
+
+Then L_b(s) is the maximum of P_b(u) minus the duration of each directed walking
+path s -> u, including the empty path. A max-priority reverse Dijkstra computes
+this closure. Positive footpath durations ensure cycles cannot increase a
+latest-ready value. Boarding consumes a layer, so equal-time inter-trip
+transfers cannot introduce an unresolved dependency within a layer.
+
+Induction: any actual suffix with no boardings is a directed walk covered by
+L_0. For an actual suffix with b>0 boardings, its access/transfer walk reaches a
+pickup-permitted event. Following the boarded vehicle until the first actual
+alighting uses consecutive connections, so the reverse chain recurrence covers
+it. Its remaining suffix has at most b-1 boardings and is covered inductively.
+The reverse walking closure therefore gives a latest-ready value at least as
+late as the actual prefix time. This proves necessity, not sufficiency.
+
+For an off-vehicle label with m boardings, reject only if its time is greater
+than L_(B-m)(stop). For an on-vehicle label, reject only if R_(B-m)(lastConnection)
+is false. The implementation stores the minimum r for which each connection's
+R_r is true. Bounds are inclusive at LatestArrival. The original resource,
+pickup/dropoff, transfer and accessibility checks still decide actual edges.
+
+Consequently no feasible full journey identity is removed. This is not a new
+prefix-dominance rule and does not replace paths by merely equal objective
+values. Existing K-prefix dominance, terminal tie ordering and top-k/cap
+certification conditions are unchanged. If context or label/journey limits
+fail, completeness is still false. Separate score-cap lanes still certify each
+at-most-boarding top-k set and union their identities as before.
+
+## Preparation cost and unmeasured tradeoff
+
+This is query-time preparation, included in existing core timing, not free
+index preprocessing. With S stops, C connections, W directed footpaths and
+B<=16 boardings, it adds B complete trip-chain passes and B reverse walking
+closures, plus copying/retaining B+1 stop-time rows. A conservative time bound
+is O(B*(C+S+(S+W)*log(S+W))); normal heap work depends on improvements. Seeds
+are queued once per improved stop rather than once per connection.
+
+Persistent extra lane storage is 8*(B+1)*S bytes for int64 latest-ready rows,
+plus C bytes for uint8 minimum additional boarding counts, slice overhead and
+transient reverse-Dijkstra heap storage. This is in addition to the preexisting
+walking/last-vehicle bound arrays. B=0 avoids the per-connection byte array.
+Stratified wrappers currently prepare independent cap lanes, so preparation and
+storage are repeated across those lanes. Shared search retains independent lane
+bounds. This may outweigh search savings on easy or dense-walking queries;
+only official-data end-to-end preparation/core/RSS measurements can decide.
+
+For B>16 the optional certificate is not built: all previously supported
+queries still use the existing exact-top-k algorithm and last-boarding bound.
+This is a preprocessing guard, not a new query cap, larger budget, unsupported
+status or reduced correctness contract. No global mutable cache is introduced.
+
+## Generic verification
+
+The candidate has direct tests for directed walking, intermediate no-pickup /
+no-dropoff stay-aboard, zero-time events, inclusive horizon, unchanged enumeration
+budgets, independent shared-lane order, stratified certificates, cancellation and
+large-boarding fallback.
+
+An isolated benchmark checkout adds independent exhaustive-oracle checks for
+all walking phases/resources, prohibited/minimum/specific transfer exceptions,
+accessibility, walking cycles, no-pickup/no-dropoff, zero-time events, input and
+lane permutations, and 128 deterministic tiny randomized seeds. Arrival tests
+compare complete identities for k=1,3,5,10; cap tests compare k=3 separately for
+every boarding cap and compare shared versus single results/counters.
+
+Source and bench full-suite outcomes and exact vendoring instructions are
+recorded in the accompanying local candidate deliverable. No remote push or
+publication is part of this work.
